\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Prior-sensitivity comparison for IMRPhenomD\_NRTidalv2\xspace  . The directly sampled flat-in-redshift posterior (teal) places substantially more mass at high \ensuremath  {H_{0}}\xspace  than the reweighted baseline posterior (dashed), and both shift to higher \ensuremath  {H_{0}}\xspace  than the baseline volumetric-distance posterior (solid). The enlarged peculiar-velocity run (dotted) is effectively indistinguishable from the baseline in this projection. Produced by \texttt  {Plots/plot\_H0\_IMRPhenomD\_reweighted.py}.}}{7}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
